  {
    "annotations": {
      "description": "Thin pool metadata exhaustion is worse than data exhaustion: the pool goes read-only or fails and needs an offline thin_check. The conservative profile sizes metadata at 128 bytes per chunk, 1 MiB per device slot and a reserve, so growth past this level means more devices than planned or snapshots. Stop new placements on the node and inspect lvs -a before metadata runs out. Never run thin_check against the live metadata device.",
